text = """LOCALLY RELEVANT APPROACH:
Lampung is famous for black pepper, coffee, and cocoa, yet yields and quality are collapsing due to unpredictable climate shocks and soil rendered hard and barren by excessive chemical inputs. Disillusioned youth migrate to cities or turn to dangerous artisanal mining. PT Klumbayan Gold Farm (KGF) addresses this crisis through regenerative agroforestry and Climate-Smart Agriculture. By minimizing chemical inputs, optimizing land use, and intercropping, we restore soil health, build resilient crops, and diversify farm income to make agriculture economically viable again.

MAIN BENEFICIARIES & STAKEHOLDERS:
1. Smallholder Farmers (1,250): Core beneficiaries across 3 regencies in Lampung, Indonesia, gaining climate resilience and income stability.
2. Women & Youth: Re-engaging young people and women to reverse rural exodus and prevent high-risk mining work.
3. Local Collectors & Supply Chain MSMEs: Integrating village collectors into transparent, fair-price trading networks.
4. Institutional Partners: Collaborating with government bodies, development agencies, universities, and research institutions to scale sustainable landscape models."""

